__label__booksjapanese kanji for beginners jlpt levels n5 n4 first steps to learn the basic japanese characters includes cd rom about the author timothy g stout lived in japan for over 20 years and has taught japanese language in public and private schools and at the university level while teaching at the american school in japan he research the use of keyword mnemonics in the instruction of japanese stout has a doctorate in education edd from utah state university an m a in japanese pedagogy from columbia university and a b a in japanese teaching from brigham young he currently teaches japanese at utah valley university and resides in lehi utah with his wife and five children stout is the author of japanese hiragana and katakana for beginners and let's learn japanese both available from tuttle
